    {
      "block_id": "2102.03334_p7_b19",
      "text": "Natural Language for Visual Reasoning.\nThe NLVR2\ntask is a binary classi\ufb01cation task given triplets of two im-\nages and a question in natural language. As there are two\ninput images unlike the pre-training setup, multiple strate-\ngies exist7. Following OSCAR (Li et al., 2020b) and VinVL\n(Zhang et al., 2021), we use the pair method. Here, the\ntriplet input is reformulated into two pairs (question, im-\nage1) and (question, image2), and each pair goes through\nthe ViLT. The head takes the concatenation of two pooled\nrepresentations (p) as input and outputs the binary predic-\ntion.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.11,
        409.65,
        291.1,
        539.25
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        220,
        1638,
        1164,
        2157
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 583,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
