      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 183,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2102.03334_p7_b29",
      "text": "It has been reported that the number of training iterations\naffects the performance of self-supervised models (Devlin\net al., 2019; Chen et al., 2020a;b). As VLP is also a form\nof self-supervised training, we examine the effects of train-\ning durations. As expected, the performance constantly\nincreases as we train the model for longer training steps\n(rows 1~3). Masking whole words for the MLM objective\n(rows 3~4) and \ufb01ne-tuning with augmentation (row 6) also\n",
      "bbox": [
